<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 6,400T of copra from Nidera.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 6,400T of copra from Nidera.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean feed millers on Tuesday bought 6,400 tonnes of copra at $116.50 a tonne C&amp;F, traders said.</p>
<p>The purchase was made from Nidera through a closed tender, they said. The buyers include Taihan Sugar Corp and the Korea Feed Association in Pusan.</p>
<p>Arrival for 3,400 tonnes was set by July 25 and for the remaining 3,000 tonnes by August 15 to the southeastern port of Ulsan.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
